WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.260
Good to have you on Tesla's short time, episode 529.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.240
I'm Patrick in Vancouver.

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:07.860
Today is July 2nd, 2026.

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:10.260
Plenty going on in EV land.

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:11.340
Let's get to it.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.580
Tesla's new winter heat patent

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:15.960
turns the compressor into a deliberate boiler

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:18.820
to protect range when ambient temperatures crash.

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:22.920
The filing details in 8-way valve and super manifold

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:26.420
that link the battery, drive train, and cabin thermal loops.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:30.620
The system scavenges motor or battery heat when available.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.620
When those sources are insufficient,

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:34.820
the compressor runs in a lossy mode

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:38.240
that boils refrigerant directly across the motor and inverter.

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:42.640
This setup eliminates the dedicated high-voltage cabin heater

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:45.940
and reduces both cost and weight at fleet scale.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:49.380
Software decides cabin versus battery priority

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:51.540
using trip length and weather forecasts.

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:55.560
Dan Ives confirmed his departure from Wedbush this week

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:57.480
after 8 years covering Tesla.

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:02.700
He expressed interest in continuing to follow TSLA and SPCX

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:03.620
at another firm.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:07.980
Ives has been a visible voice on the stock for the past 8 years.

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:12.960
The move comes as Tesla trades at $425.30.

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:17.080
No specific reasons were given for the exit in the announcement.

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:20.680
Coverage of the name will continue from his next role.

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:24.760
After seeing how Tesla squeezes efficiency from every jewel,

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:29.740
let's look at a regulatory win that also protects efficiency and reputation.

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:35.680
The National Highway Traffic Safety Administration closed its 2020 electrocreaser,

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:43.940
closed its 2022 probe into unexpected breaking on 695,000 Model 3 and Model Y vehicles.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:47.920
Complaint volume dropped from 300 at the start of the review

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:51.820
to only three incidents reported so far in 2026.

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:57.740
An early 2022 over-the-air update corrected the deceleration behavior.

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:03.220
Investigators found no evidence of lane departures or unsafe following distances

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:05.100
that could lead to rear end collisions.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:11.260
The agency closed the case without further action after determining the safety risk remained low.

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:14.760
While regulators sign off on existing vehicles,

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:19.280
Tesla is already shifting factory space toward its next hardware platform.

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:25.540
Assembly cells for Optimus are now being installed inside the Fremont factory in the area

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:28.820
formerly used for Model S and Model X production.

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:33.300
Dedicated cells are also under construction at Giga, Texas.

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:39.540
The move reflects a deliberate reallocation of manufacturing resources toward humanoid robots

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:43.600
even while the production ramp remains slower than initially targeted.

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:47.760
This is the first visible sign of factory floor progress

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:51.920
since we last discussed the program in episode 525.

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:56.800
Volume production is still expected in 2027 or later.

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:01.940
And the key open question remains when weekly output will reach hundreds of units.

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:07.980
Tesla noted it has moved from a single sports car to more than 9 million vehicles on the road.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:13.420
Five Giga factories are now operating along with the world's largest fast charging network

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:16.040
that includes over 80,000 superchargers.

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:20.600
Energy storage deployments include more than 1 million power walls

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:24.100
and 70 plus gigawatt hours of industrial projects.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:31.040
The company framed current work on autonomy and Optimus as the next phase after 23 years.

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:35.240
The reflection was posted directly from the Tesla account on X.

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:42.140
As Tesla reallocates factory real estate, its charging network is quietly setting new utilization records.

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:48.620
The supercharger network delivered a record 2.0 terawatt hours of energy in the second quarter.

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:55.680
Average daily usage reached 9 sessions per stall with almost no reported weight times at many locations.

00:03:56.340 --> 00:04:01.740
The result reflects both a larger fleet and smoother day-to-day operations across the network.

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:07.300
Strong network performance lines up with improving registration trends in key markets.

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:14.360
European registrations rose across several markets in June ahead of expected second quarter delivery numbers.

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:18.780
The increase continues the recovery trend observed in prior months.

00:04:19.420 --> 00:04:25.060
Data for the region arrives just before Tesla is scheduled to report its quarterly delivery totals.

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:30.560
Multiple countries contributed to the June uptick rather than a single standout market.

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:35.660
The figure's position Tesla for potential sequential growth in the second quarter.

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:45.120
In Australia, the model Y surpassed 8,000 units in a single month, setting a new record for any individual Tesla model in that country.

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:53.620
The surge helped Tesla maintain the top electric vehicle position in Australia, while broader EV adoption reached new highs.

00:04:54.280 --> 00:04:59.260
Export strength from other regions offset softer domestic numbers for some competitors.

00:05:00.260 --> 00:05:06.540
The 8,000-plus figure marks the first time any single Tesla model crossed that threshold in Australia.

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:11.460
Overall, EV market share gains accompanied the monthly sales peak.

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:21.440
Tesla sold more than 8,000 model Y units in Australia last month, marking the first time any single Tesla model crossed that threshold there.

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:27.920
The same month saw Tesla regain second place in Taiwan registrations after earlier softness.

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:35.000
Registrations climbed sharply in June, moving Tesla back into the number 2 spot in the island's auto market.

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:39.400
The recovery aligns with broader EV demand growth in the region.

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:47.300
In the United States, first quarter volume declined, yet Tesla still increased its share of the overall electric vehicle market.

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:53.720
The result shows competitors also faced headwinds even as Tesla's absolute numbers declined.

00:05:54.720 --> 00:06:02.160
BYD's overall sales rose 5.5% in June, even as domestic volume fell 22%.

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:05.560
Export provided the offset that kept the company on track.

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:12.460
The result positions BYD to challenge Tesla again in global fully electric volume this quarter.

00:06:13.240 --> 00:06:17.300
Lower priced models continue to gain share in markets outside China.

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:22.300
The modest growth comes amid a broader slowdown in the Chinese domestic market.

00:06:22.300 --> 00:06:28.660
While sales momentum builds, one operational headache is drawing attention at gigafactory Nevada.

00:06:29.260 --> 00:06:36.160
Multiple trailer load thefts of finished or near finished battery packs have occurred at the Nevada site in recent weeks.

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:43.400
Each load carries millions of dollars in value and creates both direct financial loss and supply chain disruption.

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:49.760
Tesla is coordinating with local authorities and reviewing perimeter and logistics security measures.

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:56.500
On the product side, a leaked photo offers the first look at a possible longer wheelbase model Y.

00:06:57.040 --> 00:07:02.240
An image circulating on X shows what appears to be an extended wheelbase body style.

00:07:02.760 --> 00:07:09.440
The photo supplies the first visual evidence supporting the long rumored L variant intended for specific markets.

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:14.960
Now, one thing worth watching is the wave of battery thefts at gigafactory Nevada.

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:21.660
The incidence target high value finished or near finished packs and have happened repeatedly in recent weeks.

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:30.300
Beyond the direct financial hit, the thefts create ongoing supply chain friction while Tesla works with authorities on security upgrades.

00:07:31.020 --> 00:07:37.440
Tesla brought in a senior semiconductor executive from Intel to accelerate its internal chip development program.

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:43.040
The higher target's next generation inference hardware under the TerraFab project.

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:48.360
The move strengthens Tesla's push to control more of its own silicon supply chain.

00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:53.860
No specific start date or role title beyond the project focus was disclosed.

00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:58.120
The addition comes as Tesla scales its in-house silicon efforts.

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:05.220
Tesla vehicles now use internal microphones to detect squeaks and rattles during final assembly checks.

00:08:05.800 --> 00:08:11.760
The microphones listen for cabin noise as each new vehicle drives itself through quality control stations.

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:15.440
The system flags issues before the car leaves the line.

00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:22.240
It extends the use of vehicle sensors already present for full self-driving into manufacturing quality control.

00:08:22.920 --> 00:08:26.260
The approach was confirmed in recent factory process updates.

00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:29.980
A model Y caught fire following a highway incident.

00:08:30.620 --> 00:08:35.720
Arrival manufacturer highlighted its own rescue efforts and public statements around the event.

00:08:35.720 --> 00:08:41.580
The episode drew attention to how competitors position safety narratives around Tesla events.

00:08:42.220 --> 00:08:47.180
No further details on injuries or the cause of the fire were released in initial reports.

00:08:48.020 --> 00:08:52.060
The publicity response from the rival drew separate commentary online.

00:08:52.760 --> 00:09:01.460
Thermal energy in an electric vehicle must be generated, moved or stored at a direct energy cost rather than appearing as free waste heat.

00:09:01.460 --> 00:09:11.720
The new patent therefore treats every jewel as a tradable asset that can be shifted between battery, motors and cabin through one eight-way valve and manifold.

00:09:12.380 --> 00:09:19.080
When no external heat is available the system intentionally reduces compressor efficiency to create heat on demand.

00:09:19.880 --> 00:09:27.120
Removing a dedicated high voltage heater from millions of vehicles lowers bill of materials cost and assembly complexity.

00:09:28.120 --> 00:09:32.740
Software decides trip by trip whether to spend or conserve that thermal capital.

00:09:33.280 --> 00:09:41.020
The same architecture works in reverse during extreme heat or fast charging by dumping surplus battery heat into an empty cabin.

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:47.020
Over time the approach tightens the connection between thermal management hardware and gross margin,

00:09:47.460 --> 00:09:51.080
because every watt hour conserved improves cost per mile.

00:09:51.080 --> 00:10:00.100
Before we go, keep an eye on further Optimus Cell installation updates from both Fremont and Giga Texas as the production footprint expands.

00:10:01.020 --> 00:10:03.500
And that's everything worth knowing about Tesla today.

00:10:03.960 --> 00:10:11.640
TSLA closed at $425.30 up $4.70 1.1%.

